thub.com/arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","login":"arkology","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107463#pullrequestreview-2922308556","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107463","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-06-12T19:08:18Z"},{"id":2943829058,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6vd0RC","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"1319ca198e571e723aed498130ac6bd0a5b850cf","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?u=8069d9b7bc6ab503ce83dfcfa53fd021672aeccf&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","login":"Mickeon","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon"},"body":"Tested. The feature seems to work fine but I noticed some differences from the script editor's equivalent:\r\n- Due of this implementation, the find bar is entirely not shared between documentation tabs. \r\n\t- This _could_ prove annoying if you don't know what you're exactly looking for.\r\n\t- The find bar remains open when another tab is selected. Coming back to the same tab restores the bar exactly as it was. In the script editor, when this happens the find bar is closed.\r\n- Toggling either \"Whole Words\" or \"Match Case\" (sometimes) resets the current match to the first. In the script editor, when toggling, the current match is only reset if it is no longer valid, and even then the very next one is focused.\r\n\t- I think this has something to do with the current match's index not being accounted for properly.\r\n- For some reason the class names written after \"Inherits:\" and \"Inherited by:\" are not accounted for with \"Whole Words\".\r\n\t- Something to do with no-break spaces?\r\n\r\n\r\nI think the most reliable way to test this that I've found is searching for \"Object\" in **Node**'s class reference.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107463#pullrequestreview-2943829058","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107463","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-06-19T18:52:49Z"}]